@startuml
title DEV2 Cases - Submission, AI Review, Allocation and Critical Close

autonumber

actor "Citizen" as Citizen
actor "EmergencyCoordinator /\nCaseManager" as Staff
actor "LogisticsManager" as Logistics
actor "SystemAdmin" as Admin

participant "RequestsController" as ReqCtrl
participant "IRequestService /\nRequestService" as ReqSvc
participant "IRequestWorkflowService /\nRequestWorkflowService" as Workflow
participant "IRequestMergeService /\nRequestStatusService" as StatusSvc
participant "RequestStateMachine" as StateMachine
participant "CaseWriteHelper" as Writer
participant "ICloseCaseDecisionGate" as Gate
participant "CmsDbContext" as Db
participant "AuditEventsController" as AuditCtrl
participant "NotificationsController" as NotifyCtrl
participant "RecommendationController (M3)" as RecCtrl
participant "DecisionController (M3)" as DecisionCtrl
participant "OperationsController (M4)" as OpsCtrl

note over ReqCtrl, Db
  Runtime prerequisite: backend/src/Cms.Api/Modules/CasesModule.cs is empty.
  Member 1 must call Cms.Infrastructure.Cases.CasesModuleExtensions.AddCasesModule
  or Cases controller activation fails with a DI resolution error.
  Only NullRequestReader, NoOpRequestStatusService and DenyAllDecisionGate
  have fail-closed fallbacks.
end note

== Citizen request submission ==

Citizen -> ReqCtrl : POST /api/v1/requests (CreateRequestDto)
ReqCtrl -> ReqSvc : SubmitAsync(request)
ReqSvc -> ReqSvc : Validate ApprovedCategories\nand area/crisis match
ReqSvc -> Db : Set<Area>().FirstOrDefaultAsync(AreaId)
ReqSvc -> ReqSvc : Protect(AccessibilityNeeds)\nStatus = RequestStatus.Submitted
ReqSvc -> Db : IRequestRepository.AddAsync(Request)
ReqSvc -> Writer : AddHistoryAsync(Submitted -> Submitted,\nreason = "Request submitted")
ReqSvc -> Writer : AddAuditAsync("Request.Submitted",\n"Request", id, details, userId)
ReqSvc -> Writer : AddOutboxAsync("Request.Submitted",\nid, payload, idempotencyKey)
ReqSvc -> Db : SaveChangesAsync()
ReqCtrl --> Citizen : 201 Created { id }

== AI recommendations appear; request status unchanged ==

Staff -> RecCtrl : POST /api/recommendation/crisis/{crisisId}/generate
RecCtrl --> Staff : 200 OK { recommendationId }
Staff -> RecCtrl : GET /api/recommendation/{recommendationId}
RecCtrl --> Staff : 200 OK (recommendation; advisory only)
Staff -> ReqCtrl : GET /api/v1/requests/{id}
ReqCtrl --> ReqSvc : GetDetailAsync(id)
ReqSvc --> ReqCtrl : RequestDetailDto (still Submitted)
ReqCtrl --> Staff : 200 OK (status unchanged)

note over RecCtrl
  No GET /api/v1/recommendations?targetId= endpoint exists.
  Recommendation generation must not mutate request status.
end note

== Verify then triage ==

Staff -> ReqCtrl : POST /api/v1/requests/{id}/transition\n{"to":"Verified","reason":"Verified against call centre record."}
ReqCtrl -> Workflow : TransitionAsync(id, Verified, reason, null)
Workflow -> StatusSvc : TransitionAsync(id, Verified, reason, null)
StatusSvc -> StateMachine : Ensure(Submitted, Verified)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddHistoryAsync(Submitted -> Verified)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddAuditAsync("Request.StatusChanged")
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddNotificationAsync(id, requesterUserId,\n"request.status.Verified", data, version, ct)
StatusSvc -> Db : SaveChangesAsync()
ReqCtrl --> Staff : 204 No Content

Staff -> ReqCtrl : POST /api/v1/requests/{id}/transition\n{"to":"Triaged","reason":"Food priority set."}
ReqCtrl -> Workflow : TransitionAsync(id, Triaged, reason, null)
Workflow -> StatusSvc : TransitionAsync(id, Triaged, reason, null)
StatusSvc -> StateMachine : Ensure(Verified, Triaged)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddHistoryAsync(Verified -> Triaged)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddAuditAsync("Request.StatusChanged")
StatusSvc -> Db : SaveChangesAsync()
ReqCtrl --> Staff : 204 No Content

== Coordinator verification and status transition ==

Staff -> ReqCtrl : POST /api/v1/requests/{id}/transition\n(TransitionRequestDto)
ReqCtrl -> Workflow : TransitionAsync(id, request)
Workflow -> StatusSvc : TransitionAsync(id, To, Reason, DecisionId)
StatusSvc -> Db : Set<Request>().FirstOrDefaultAsync(id)

alt to = Closed AND urgency = Critical
    StatusSvc -> Gate : IsApprovedAsync(decisionId, requestId, ct)
    alt approved
        Gate --> StatusSvc : true
    else denied / missing decision
        Gate --> StatusSvc : false
        StatusSvc --> ReqCtrl : ForbiddenException\nCLOSE_DECISION_REQUIRED
        ReqCtrl --> Staff : 403 Forbidden
    end
end

StatusSvc -> StateMachine : Ensure(currentStatus, to)
StatusSvc -> Writer : NextRequestVersionAsync(requestId)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddHistoryAsync(from -> to,\nchangedByUserId, reason)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddAuditAsync("Request.StatusChanged",\n"Request", id, details, userId)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddNotificationAsync(requestId,\nrequesterUserId, "request.status.{to}", data, version, ct)
StatusSvc -> Db : SaveChangesAsync()
ReqCtrl --> Staff : 204 No Content

note over Gate
  DEV2 DecisionGateCloseCaseAdapter delegates to
  IDecisionGate.RequireApprovedAsync(decisionId,
  RecommendationType.CloseCase, requestId, ct).
  It is fail-closed until Member 3 implements and
  registers the real IDecisionGate.
end note

== Human decision and allocation handoff ==

Staff -> DecisionCtrl : POST /api/decision\n{"recommendationId": "...", "outcome": "Approved",\n"finalPayloadJson": "{\"requestId\":\"...\",\"inventoryId\":\"42000000-...0001\",\"quantity\":1}"}
DecisionCtrl --> Staff : 201 Created { decisionId }
Staff -> OpsCtrl : GET /api/v1/recommendations/match/resources/{id}
OpsCtrl --> Staff : 200 OK (ranked candidates and explanations)
Staff -> OpsCtrl : POST /api/v1/allocations\nIdempotency-Key: uat-alloc-{id}\n{"decisionId":"..."}
OpsCtrl --> Staff : 201 Created { status: "Allocated" }
Staff -> ReqCtrl : POST /api/v1/requests/{id}/transition\n{"to":"Allocated","decisionId":"..."}
ReqCtrl -> Workflow : TransitionAsync(id, Allocated, reason, decisionId)
Workflow -> StatusSvc : TransitionAsync(id, Allocated, reason, decisionId)
StatusSvc -> StateMachine : Ensure(Approved, Allocated)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddAuditAsync("Request.StatusChanged")
StatusSvc -> Db : SaveChangesAsync()
ReqCtrl --> Staff : 204 No Content

note over DecisionCtrl, OpsCtrl
  M3 and M4 owned endpoints. Allocation currently checks
  DecisionOutcome.Approve/Modify while the enum defines
  Approved/Modified; report this integration issue, do not fix here.
end note

== Critical close with CloseCase decision ==

Staff -> ReqCtrl : POST /api/v1/requests/{criticalId}/transition\n{"to":"Closed","decisionId":"..."}
ReqCtrl -> Workflow : TransitionAsync(criticalId, Closed, reason, decisionId)
Workflow -> StatusSvc : TransitionAsync(criticalId, Closed, reason, decisionId)
StatusSvc -> Gate : IsApprovedAsync(decisionId, criticalId, ct)
StatusSvc -> StateMachine : Ensure(Fulfilled, Closed)
alt approved CloseCase decision
    Gate --> StatusSvc : true
    StatusSvc -> Writer : AddHistoryAsync(Fulfilled -> Closed)
    StatusSvc -> Writer : AddAuditAsync("Request.StatusChanged")
    StatusSvc -> Writer : AddNotificationAsync(criticalId,\nrequesterUserId, "request.status.Closed", data, version, ct)
    StatusSvc -> Db : SaveChangesAsync()
    ReqCtrl --> Staff : 204 No Content
else denied or missing decisionId
    Gate --> StatusSvc : false
    StatusSvc --> ReqCtrl : ForbiddenException CLOSE_DECISION_REQUIRED
    ReqCtrl --> Staff : 403 Forbidden; status remains Fulfilled
end

== Assignment ==

Staff -> ReqCtrl : PATCH /api/v1/requests/{id}/assign\n(AssignRequestDto)
ReqCtrl -> ReqSvc : AssignAsync(id, request)
ReqSvc -> Db : Set<Request>().FirstOrDefaultAsync(id)
ReqSvc -> ReqSvc : EnsureStaff()
ReqSvc -> ReqSvc : AssignedToUserId = request.AssignedToUserId
ReqSvc -> Writer : AddAuditAsync("Request.Assigned",\n"Request", id, details, userId)
ReqSvc -> Db : SaveChangesAsync()
ReqCtrl --> Staff : 204 No Content

== Merge ==

Staff -> ReqCtrl : POST /api/v1/requests/{id}/merge\n(MergeRequestDto)
ReqCtrl -> StatusSvc : MergeAsync(sourceId, targetRequestId, reason)
StatusSvc -> Db : Load source and target Request
StatusSvc -> StateMachine : Ensure(source.Status, Merged,\nhasMergeTarget = true)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddHistoryAsync(source Merged)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddHistoryAsync(target unchanged)
StatusSvc -> Db : Set<RequestLink>().AddAsync(Merged)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddAuditAsync("Request.Merged")
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddAuditAsync("Request.MergeTarget")
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddNotificationAsync(source.Id, sourceRequester,\n"request.status.Merged", data, sourceVersion, ct)
StatusSvc -> Writer : AddNotificationAsync(target.Id, targetRequester,\n"request.status.Merged", data, targetVersion, ct)
StatusSvc -> Db : SaveChangesAsync()
ReqCtrl --> Staff : 204 No Content

== Timeline and cross-member verification ==

Citizen -> ReqCtrl : GET /api/v1/requests/{id}/timeline
ReqCtrl -> ReqSvc : GetTimelineAsync(id)
ReqSvc -> Db : Query RequestStatusHistory\nand identity.Users
ReqCtrl --> Citizen : 200 OK (RequestTimelineEntryDto list)

Admin -> AuditCtrl : GET /api/v1/audit-events
AuditCtrl --> Admin : 200 OK (shared audit trail)
Staff -> AuditCtrl : GET /api/v1/audit-events
AuditCtrl --> Staff : 403 Forbidden (AdminOnly policy)

Citizen -> NotifyCtrl : GET /api/v1/notifications
NotifyCtrl --> Citizen : 200 OK (in-app inbox)

note over NotifyCtrl
  Inbox delivery depends on the Member 1/Member 3
  outbox processor consuming Notification.Send messages.
end note

@enduml
